WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:13.995
<v Narrator>Welcome to Once Upon a Time Show. It's time for a bedtime story. Hello, little one. Snuggle down under your blanket, nice and warm.

2
00:00:14.295 --> 00:00:20.225
<v Narrator>Tonight's story is a very old one. It's one of Aesop's fables, and we tell it in our own words.

3
00:00:20.525 --> 00:00:26.454
<v Narrator>It's about a fast hare, a slow tortoise and a big race. Are you ready? Let's begin.

4
00:00:26.754 --> 00:00:35.923
<v Narrator>Once upon a time, in a green meadow, there lived a hare. He had long ears and long legs, and he could run very, very fast.

5
00:00:36.223 --> 00:00:46.704
<v Narrator>In the same meadow lived a tortoise. She had a round, hard shell on her back. She walked slowly, one little step at a time. Step, step, step.

6
00:00:47.004 --> 00:00:54.083
<v Narrator>One day, Hare laughed at Tortoise. You're so slow, he said. Do you ever get anywhere at all?

7
00:00:54.383 --> 00:01:01.927
<v Narrator>Tortoise smiled. Yes, I do, she said. And I get there sooner than you think. Let's run a race, and you'll see.

8
00:01:08.227 --> 00:01:14.331
<v Narrator>Hare thought this was very funny. A race with a tortoise? But he said yes, just for fun.

9
00:01:14.631 --> 00:01:23.505
<v Narrator>Fox came along to help. He marked a path across the meadow, from the old oak tree to the little blue pond. The pond was the finish line.

10
00:01:23.805 --> 00:01:33.136
<v Narrator>Ready, said Fox. Set. Go! Whoosh! Hare zoomed off like the wind. Tortoise set off too. Step, step, step.

11
00:01:38.436 --> 00:01:49.858
<v Narrator>Soon Hare was far, far ahead. He looked back. Tortoise was just a tiny dot. Hare gave a big yawn. I have lots of time, he said. I'll take a little nap.

12
00:01:50.158 --> 00:01:59.408
<v Narrator>So Hare lay down in the soft grass, under a shady bush. He closed his eyes, and soon he was fast asleep. Snore, snore.

13
00:01:59.708 --> 00:02:11.384
<v Narrator>But Tortoise didn't stop. Step, step, step. Slow and steady. She walked right past the bush where Hare was sleeping. And Hare slept on, quiet and still.

14
00:02:11.684 --> 00:02:20.981
<v Narrator>At last, Hare woke up. He stretched and rubbed his eyes. Then he looked far down the path. Oh no! Tortoise was almost at the blue pond!

15
00:02:27.281 --> 00:02:37.123
<v Narrator>Hare ran as fast as he could. Faster, faster! But it was too late. Tortoise took one last little step, and she was over the finish line.

16
00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:47.869
<v Narrator>Tortoise had won the race! Fox clapped his paws. Hare puffed and panted. Then he smiled a small smile. Well done, he said. You really did get there.

17
00:02:48.169 --> 00:02:58.395
<v Narrator>Tortoise smiled back. Slow and steady, she said softly. That's my way. And Hare learned something that day. The fastest one doesn't always win the race.

18
00:03:05.695 --> 00:03:14.725
<v Narrator>And now the meadow is quiet. The sun is going down, and the sky is pink and gold. Fox curls up in his cozy den.

19
00:03:15.025 --> 00:03:22.661
<v Narrator>Hare lies down in the soft grass. Tortoise tucks her head into her warm shell. The little pond goes shh, shh.

20
00:03:22.961 --> 00:03:35.230
<v Narrator>Close your eyes now, little one. Slow and steady, breathe in, breathe out. Step, step, step, all the way to sleep. Goodnight from Once Upon a Time Show. Sweet dreams.
